diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 71b051dc..75ca6946 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -133,8 +133,11 @@ the first-token wait. It cannot reveal router retries or account cooldowns absen
 Remote sources and agents appear alongside local sources in the native dashboard and history when available. Remote
 data does not include categorized today's token totals, project paths, traffic or a continuous live chart; unavailable
 values, including missing price data, remain unknown. History is aggregated in the viewer's time zone, requested by
-the client from the collector. Partial log reads are marked as potentially incomplete. Remote network and performance
-history are unavailable; disconnected intervals remain gaps rather than continuous measurements.
+the client from the collector. Partial log reads are marked as potentially incomplete. Supported collectors provide
+remote performance scores and host-specific baselines, plus real daily performance history from analyzed logs. A
+baseline uses the collector host's local dates; history uses the viewer's time zone, so day boundaries can differ.
+Older collectors without performance fields leave it unavailable while their other data remains usable. Remote network
+history is unavailable, and disconnected intervals remain gaps rather than continuous measurements.
 After the client requests its time zone, snapshot today totals also use that zone. Untagged or null-zone snapshots
 retain collector-local compatibility behavior. History from older collectors without a matching time-zone tag is
 unavailable rather than being mislabeled as viewer-local.
